## What I built (9 files, `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/TripReplayCharts.*`)
A production SwiftUI + Swift Charts port of `features/trips/components/TripReplayCharts.tsx`, following the established `SocChart`/`DriveOverviewChart`/`ElevationChart` conventions:
- **Dual-axis area chart** — speed (left, user unit) + power (right, kW) as two overlapping `AreaMark(stacking:.unstacked)`+`LineMark` series; power projected onto the speed scale with a trailing kW axis (Swift Charts carries one y-scale/chart).
- **Playhead + seek** — dashed `RuleMark` at `currentIndex`; `.chartXSelection`→`scrub`→`nearestIndexByTime` (line-for-line port incl. the web tie-break)→`onSeek(originIndex)`, de-duplicated like the web `lastForwardedRef`.
- **Every state** — loading / empty / error / stale / offline / content; all 6 source i18n keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade; `view.opened` telemetry; VoiceOver labels; tokens only (P1/S9).

